Raj Kandala is a Postdoctoral Research Associate at the University of Reading, working within the AFESP project “VaaSS — Vegetation as a Soil Sensor.” His research focuses on advancing land surface modelling, with particular emphasis on unified hydro-thermal theory, vegetation–soil interactions, parameter estimation, and data assimilation. He works to improve the representation of soil and vegetation processes in land surface models, with the goal of enhancing the accuracy of weather and climate prediction systems.

Raj holds a PhD from the Indian Institute of Science, Bangalore, where his doctoral work centred on estimating profile soil moisture, soil temperature, and soil hydraulic and thermal parameters using the Ensemble Kalman Filter.
